PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_11lmgp_cython_7solvers_6L0_LMG_deblur, "\n    Image restoration with L0 gradient prior and LMG prior.\n    Equivalent to MATLAB L0_LMG_deblur.m \342\200\224 the core of the LMG paper.\n\n    Solves (via half-quadratic splitting / ADMM):\n        min_S  ||S*k - B||^2  +  lambda * ||2 - G_S(S)||_1\n               + wei_grad * ||nabla S||_0\n\n    where G_S is the Local Maximum Gradient operator (Eq. 3-4 of the paper).\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    Im                    : (H, W) blurred image (ALREADY boundary-wrapped)\n    kernel                : (kh, kw) blur kernel\n    lambda_lmg            : weight for LMG prior\n    wei_grad              : weight for L0 gradient prior\n    kappa                 : ADM update ratio (default 2.0)\n    lmg_denoise_eps       : float or None \342\200\224 guided filter eps / enable flag\n                            for bilateral. None = no denoising.\n    lmg_denoise_radius    : int \342\200\224 guided filter radius (default 2)\n    lmg_denoise_type      : 'guided' | 'bilateral' \342\200\224 which denoiser before LMG\n    lmg_bilateral_sigma_s : float \342\200\224 bilateral spatial sigma (default 2.0)\n    lmg_bilateral_sigma_r : float \342\200\224 bilateral range sigma (default 0.1)\n    use_soft_threshold    : bool \342\200\224 use L1 soft threshold instead of L0 hard\n                            threshold on gradients (default False)\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    S : (H, W) restored image (same size as Im, caller must crop)\n\n    CRITICAL: The LMG sparse operator uses COLUMN-MAJOR (Fortran) ordering.\n    All flatten/reshape in this function use order='F'.\n    ");
